  "body": "# v0.16.2: safer setup errors and current notebook chat requests\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Empty or whitespace-only MCP client config files can now be initialized. Malformed JSON and TOML files remain untouched and are reported clearly. `nlm setup list` continues past an unreadable client config, while `nlm setup add` and `nlm setup remove` show the affected path instead of a traceback (#400).\n- Notebook chat sends the current 9-slot consumer request while preserving Enterprise behavior (#398). Live checks covered fresh conversations, follow-ups, selected sources, and citations. The previous request format also worked during verification, so treat this as a compatibility update rather than a confirmed fix for a production failure.\n\n### Credits\n\nThanks to @pengqun for #400 and the report in #399, and to @saariuslystoned for #398.\n",
